: all checks passed.\n\nWhat changed:\n- **New `_Level` filter:** holds a handler to its floor, but also passes INFO records from `sensei_top.llm` and its submodules. `sensei_top.llmx` does not pass.\n- **Console handler:** now at INFO, filtered to ERROR, or WARNING with `--verbose`.\n- **File handler:** at DEBUG with `--verbose`, otherwise INFO. Without `--verbose` the `_Level(WARNING)` filter goes on after the header line is written, so the header still gets in.\n- **Module docstring:** the \"Levels\" bullet now says both handlers also take `sensei_top.llm`'s INFO lines.\n\nI did not run the full suite or the dashboard checks. The spec only lists `test_logs.py` and ruff, and this change touches only `logs.py`.", "ttft_ms": 1449, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 14902, "uuid": "8767803e-f5ea-4c6d-af71-c48590090a68", "ttft_stream_ms": 1123, "time_to_request_ms": 245, "first_content_frame_ms": 1124, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
